                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I thought this would let me experience being born in VR. That sounded sorta interesting and educational but that's not at all what you get.\n\nThis is a 10 minute VR movie. You're a fetus in the womb - this part is very cool for a minute as you look around and get bathed in blue light from an ultrasound. You hear fairly innane dialogue but it's fine because you're in VR in a womb and it's fun to just gaze.\n\nThen things weird. I won't spoil the story but the thumbs down is for the laughably bad animation, models and effects combined with the complete lack of interaction and short length. As demo's go you will definitely not use this to show off VR when people come over. It's not scary, educational or interesting so I'm just not sure what it's for.\n[url=https://oldgrizzledgamers.com/reviews/37th-week-pc-vr-review-fetus-feels-lot-like-wasting-10-minutes-life-32/]Full review[/url] available but it doesn't say much more than this.",
